{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/547391-hunter-the-seventh-generation","id":547391,"title":"Hunter: the Seventh Generation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-09T12:09:42-07:00","id":547391,"title":"Hunter: the Seventh Generation","content":"after giving it a lot of thought, I came to a conclusion- the Lucifuge should, thematically, be a Major Template. I mean, they are born into their lineage, their Becoming sounds very similar to the changing process the rest of the splats experience, and they have the potential to live more then any regular human, with that longevity being tied to a defining trait (their Status). They do need some reversion before doing so- both mechanically and fluff wise.<br /> <br /> so this is my idea. Feedback is always welcomed.<br /> <br /> Virtue/Vice- I don't think that part needs to be changed, although their Vice should get a bit more focus, as a representation of their &quot;inner demon&quot;<br /> <br /> Morality trait- or are we going to call it Integrity now? What ever. Anyway, I while I think that regular Integrity could work, importing the Spiritual Purity from Mirrors sounds like a good idea.<br /> <br /> X splat- Lineages. In this version, Hell is a broad term, and there are demons everywhere. Sure, there should be a &quot;pure&quot; Infernal Lineage, but it is truly not the only one. Goblins have sneaked into houses and tricked mortal men and women to sleep with them. Dark beings with no name have came through the cracks in reality and spawned their progeny. Demon Gods stalk the Shadow of the world, forcing mortal followers to be their concubines. The unquiet dead reach out of their grave, creating an unholy abomination which defies all gods and all nature. Broken pieces of the once great machine wear a fake skin, and give truth to false life. Fae, Abyssal Beings, dark spirits, vampires, demons, lilithim and many other beings have all spawned families of monsters- and the Children of the 7th Generation now need to deal with the demons who gave birth to them.<br /> <br /> Y splat- Cults (temporary name). Under that paradigm, the Lucifuge is only one group among many. The Lenfant Diabolique are another. The Silent Imperative and the Rampant are another groups of demon blooded individuals bonded together for a common goal. Each has its own ideology, goals and philosophy- but two things are common. First, each is centered around a strong, individual character- it may be the Lady, it may be the Chaldeans The only thing that is important is that the Cult is founded by someone, and that someone seems to draw others toward her. The other common feature is that each such Cult has 666 members- if this is an intentional feature or an inborn one is left to debate. This is going to include the rules for creating your own Cults, and &quot;Cultic Ascension&quot;- that is, establishing a new Cult around you, and enjoying that benefit.<br /> <br /> Z-splat- Patron. While Lineages may be tracked into a breed of demons, each Child has a single progenitor- the ancient demon who has spawned you for its enjoyment, long term planning or both. Moloch, Lilith, Abaddon, Azazel, Lucifer, Ravana, Tezcatlipoca- there are many demonic creatures who could birth your Lineage, and by defining their traits in your blood you also draw their power into your body and soul.<br /> <br /> powers &amp; sorcery- Castigation are, thematically, more of a Sorcery power then an innate power, and I think that the 5 power limitation should be kept, but the power level of their rites should be moved up. For innate powers, I think that Inferno could give some inspiration for demonic style powers, if not importing Vestments right from it.<br /> <br /> Resistance trait- yes, I know you may not like it, but I think that using Status (that is, your Cult's) should be the Resistance state. In this paradigm, your place in the Cult is everything for you- it decides how long you are going to live (unless someone is going to kill you, of course), and represent your Rank when dealing with demons. Reaching for Status above 5 means you start your own Cult and spawn 666 members to be drawn to your Cult. That means that the number of Cults in existence limits the number of possible Children around the world. At that level, you actually BECOME the organization, using the other agents in order to interact with other Cults and fight for control. This may explain why the Lucifuge is so obsessed with destroying demon cults- have too many believers centered around someone, and 666 new monsters would rise out of no where, when the ancient genes would awake. Until then, you draw from the Cult's faith and connection around you to rise in power. Still, you don't have to spawn a new Cult when you hit Status above 5- you can also challenge the former ruler for control. And yeah, this is going to need some reversion from Exp and similar mechanics, and may even have another name, but it is going to serve as something like the Status merit.<br /> <br /> so- any thoughts/suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T14:08:17-07:00","id":547502,"title":"","content":"I would argue that they fit in as a Minor Template, at best. I mean, all the other Major templates are Hammer Horror monsters, or cover a <i>large</i> thematic space. Changelings cover <i>all kinds</i> of faery tales, Sin-Eaters cover all ghost stories, Demons are spy stories, Hunter is monster hunters (which are in pretty much all fiction that includes monsters).<br /> <br /> &quot;Descendents of Demons&quot; isn't a broad enough theme, in my mind.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm a bit biased; I would prefer to see more Minor Templates than Major Templates. The latter category has too much mechanical baggage, in my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T14:56:39-07:00","id":547569,"title":"","content":"I'd have to agree with Amechra. After all, I believe Castigation, like other Endowments, is priced as Merits would be. Really, all you'd need to do is create a &quot;Core Merit&quot;(or alter Lucifuge Status to fit) that allows you the Template, some sort of &quot;fuel&quot;, and a way to acquire such &quot;fuel&quot;. <br /> <br /> Never the less, it might be fun to work them up like this. I might do it a bit differently, however. <br /> <br /> \u2022X-Splat: While I might still call it Lineage, I'd focus on the <i>characteristics</i> of the parent rather than the <i>type</i>, probably using the Seven Deadly Sins as a model. For example, those of the Aamonic Lineage(Wrath) are descended from the Warlords, Destroyers, and Brutes of Below, and their children inherit their quick temper and their skill at inflicting and surviving injury.<br /> <br /> \u2022Y-Splat: In this case, I'd probably go with philosophies rather than organizations. The Truth, the Denial, and the Reconciliation all seem like good places to start; it shouldn't be too hard to add two or four more options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T15:13:22-07:00","id":547584,"title":"","content":"I agree, they should be a minor template. At most they could become a middle of the road template like the Kitsune; but I think a minor template would work best.<br /> <br /> Integrity could become Corruption; which starts low and rises if you roll too well on Castigation. Indulge your Vice too easily. Can be deliberately increased to refill your Vice via a ritual. High Corruption makes you more powerful, but comes with various demonic problems - loss of Virtue, holy water burns, etc. The Lucifuge punishes it's members for letting Corruption get too high.<br /> <br /> Energy stat would be Vice and work like Mummy's Pillar like trait. It's refilled by indulging that particular Vice or tempting others into that particular Vice. Though the Lucifgue as an organistion encourages harmless uses of Vice. Hire prostitues for Lust, don't seduce naieve teenagers with your infernal charms. Wrath must be directed at monsters, etc.<br /> <br /> Castigation remains mostly unchanged, though I would like to create the idea of &quot;packages&quot; which are multiple Castigation powers that come as one (like demon summoning &amp; demon controlling) that only count as 1 towards your 5 maximum. Convert Willpower costs into Vice points.<br /> <br /> The only splats would be Lucifuge or Les Infants Diabolique; though Krewe like rules for building your own could be provided (a Lucifuge agent with their own cult of Hunters makes sense. There's only 666 so extra manpower has to come from somewhere)<br /> <br /> And bob's your uncle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/547391-hunter-the-seventh-generation#post547391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">X splat- Lineages. In this version, Hell is a broad term, and there are demons everywhere. Sure, there should be a &quot;pure&quot; Infernal Lineage, but it is truly not the only one.</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't. By that logic Werewolves and Beasts are both part of the Lucifgue splat. In addition the core theme isn't &quot;my parents are evil&quot; it's dealing with the demon inside of you and understanding the similartiy between yourself and those you hunt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T02:07:25-07:00","id":548170,"title":"","content":"Joining a cult can get you telepathy or telekinesis or the ability to gain an essence pool, numina, and revenant status upon death, but gaining longevity through an organization is so impressive that it make one a template? I don't really see the logic there. <br /> <br /> Then there's the fact that there is no template that is incompatible with demonic power (according to Inferno), and there is no template that actually changes one's genetic structure, you'd be making a template that is stackable with everything, which isn't how templates work. Even wolf-blooded and stigmatics (according to word of god) lose stuff in a transformation. <br /> <br /> So if you're going to do this, you need to make it worthwhile- Templates have innate advantages, not just learnable powers. <br /> <br /> Just slapping the title template on the lucifuge is just sloppy being a template is about being innately different, not learning a few tricks, or else all third tier hunters and muggles with supernatural merits would be templates.<br /> <br /> So if you want to make them a template, kick it into high gear. What's the concept? Off hand, they'd be demons in human flesh. Then they should have essence pools, infernal rank which determines their attributes, longevity, and supernatural resistance. How would they fill their essence? Can they see spirits, can they lie perfectly, can they step sideways, if they're a template then they need to be different from some schmuck off the street who made a demonic pact or two. <br /> <br /> And of course, you're hacking the setting. No more lucifuge slashers, if the conspiracies let lucifuge in, then that indicates other supernaturals are allowed in too. if the lucifuge get all hunter benefits, then so can every other supernatural. Mages with tactics anyone? Werewolves risking willpower? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:44:50-07:00","id":549011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/547391-hunter-the-seventh-generation#post547391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">X splat- Lineages. In this version, Hell is a broad term, and there are demons everywhere. Sure, there should be a &quot;pure&quot; Infernal Lineage, but it is truly not the only one. Goblins have sneaked into houses and tricked mortal men and women to sleep with them. Dark beings with no name have came through the cracks in reality and spawned their progeny. Demon Gods stalk the Shadow of the world, forcing mortal followers to be their concubines. The unquiet dead reach out of their grave, creating an unholy abomination which defies all gods and all nature. Broken pieces of the once great machine wear a fake skin, and give truth to false life. Fae, Abyssal Beings, dark spirits, vampires, demons, lilithim and many other beings have all spawned families of monsters- and the Children of the 7th Generation now need to deal with the demons who gave birth to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't favour this. These beings are all metaphysically distinct, often unrelated, and liable to produce very different effects in their children - <i>Castigations</i> are definitely infernal in tone, and I think the Lucifuge should be too, one and all. Instead, I think the X-splat should be Vice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Y splat- Cults (temporary name). Under that paradigm, the Lucifuge is only one group among many. The Lenfant Diabolique are another. The Silent Imperative and the Rampant are another groups of demon blooded individuals bonded together for a common goal. Each has its own ideology, goals and philosophy- but two things are common. First, each is centered around a strong, individual character- it may be the Lady, it may be the Chaldeans The only thing that is important is that the Cult is founded by someone, and that someone seems to draw others toward her. The other common feature is that each such Cult has 666 members- if this is an intentional feature or an inborn one is left to debate. This is going to include the rules for creating your own Cults, and &quot;Cultic Ascension&quot;- that is, establishing a new Cult around you, and enjoying that benefit. </div> </div> </div>This works, though.<br /> <br /> Resistance trait- yes, I know you may not like it, but I think that using Status (that is, your Cult's) should be the Resistance state. In this paradigm, your place in the Cult is everything for you- it decides how long you are going to live (unless someone is going to kill you, of course), and represent your Rank when dealing with demons. Reaching for Status above 5 means you start your own Cult and spawn 666 members to be drawn to your Cult. That means that the number of Cults in existence limits the number of possible Children around the world. At that level, you actually BECOME the organization, using the other agents in order to interact with other Cults and fight for control. This may explain why the Lucifuge is so obsessed with destroying demon cults- have too many believers centered around someone, and 666 new monsters would rise out of no where, when the ancient genes would awake.[/QUOTE]This works. In narrative terms, it might sometimes be the other way round - someone develops more resistance, and gains status as a consequence. I think there ought to be fuel stat in this case, maybe bounded by Resolve or Composure (the way ghouls can have vitae up to Stamina).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T08:49:02-07:00","id":710668,"title":"","content":"May I present this as another suggestion?<br /> <br /> New Advantage: Hellbound (o to ooooo)<br /> - From the moment their infernal blood manifests itself, Children of the Seventh Generation soon learn that they are starting to change into something more (and less) than human. While this causes some to shy away and deny the power in their blood, many choose to embrace their demonic lineage and actively cultivate the gifts it offers them. Depending on the circumstances, such individuals either garner the attention of the Lady of Milan, or fall in with the likes of L'Enfantes Diabolique.<br /> <br /> A Child's dots in Hellbound confer the following advantages.<ul><li>They increase the potency of passive Infernal Aspects, and are added to the dice pools of those which require rolls to activate.</li> <li>They provide a passive resistance to supernatural powers.</li> <li>They determine the character's honorary Infernal Rank</li> </ul>On a related note, I was thinking of reimagining Lucifuge Castigations and Infernal Aspects from Inferno to make them similar to Shadow and Wolf Gifts from Werewolf 2E, or to the Demon Form traits of the Unchained. More to come on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T09:26:27-07:00","id":710760,"title":"","content":"Similar thoughts. If Vice is being tracked separately (like for Possessed in Inferno), modeling Castigations on Werewolf's Gifts, or Mummy's Utterances makes sense. You can have one power with multiple facets depending on the Vice used to fuel it.<br /> <br /> Actually, Mummy's systems have a good amount of utility here. Affinities are a good template for Demonic Nature/Legacy based stuff, and Utterances for willful/learned/applied use of power. Scaled down, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T15:38:38-07:00","id":711356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/547391-hunter-the-seventh-generation?p=710760#post710760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similar thoughts. If Vice is being tracked separately (like for Possessed in Inferno), modeling Castigations on Werewolf's Gifts, or Mummy's Utterances makes sense. You can have one power with multiple facets depending on the Vice used to fuel it.<br /> <br /> Actually, Mummy's systems have a good amount of utility here. Affinities are a good template for Demonic Nature/Legacy based stuff, and Utterances for willful/learned/applied use of power. Scaled down, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're going for using the Seven Capital Sins as the Vices with regards to restructured Castigations, then yes. That works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}